# VaViM inference environment (valeoai/VideoActionModel 738050e, 2025-06-04): the inference subset of the official
# pyproject.toml at its pins, Linux x86_64, CPython 3.10, torch 2.4.0 (the README's recommended version; PyPI CUDA 12.1
# build, kernels to sm_90). The kit imports vam/video_pretraining (mup_gpt2.py and, through the package __init__,
# next_token_predictor.py), which needs torch, einops, mup, tqdm, hydra-core, lightning and omegaconf. einops is imported
# by mup_gpt2.py but not declared by the official pyproject (it came with the authors' cluster PyTorch module).
# mup: the official dependency is the unpinned git main of microsoft/mup; pinned here to its last commit 1981497
# (2023-10-20) as a hash-checked archive (inference code identical to PyPI mup 1.0.0: layer.py, infshape.py, init.py
# unchanged; shape.py only a comment; optim.py adds decoupled_wd, used in training only).
# torchvision 0.19.0 (official [torch] extra: torchvision>=0.19.0) is used only by the CPU tests to run the official
# vam/datalib/transforms.py as the reference for the input normalisation and the uint8 rule.
# Left out (training, data preparation, evaluation or notebooks only; never imported on the kit's path): jupyter, plotly,
# prettytable, clean-fid, hyperqueue, GitPython (optional import), torchdata nightly, pyquaternion, colorlog, pillow.
torch==2.4.0
torchvision==0.19.0
lightning==2.4.0
torchmetrics==1.4.3
hydra-core==1.3.2
mup @ https://github.com/microsoft/mup/archive/19814971934ef91dd546f88e913fc963e096d11c.tar.gz
einops==0.8.1
tqdm
numpy==1.26.4
